{
  "id": "heartgold-collection-and-soulsilver-collection-launch-campaign",
  "name": "HeartGold Collection and SoulSilver Collection launch campaign",
  "category": "product_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "The launch campaign for HeartGold Collection and SoulSilver Collection, the first expansions of the Pokémon Card Game LEGEND series, released in Japan on 9 October 2009. From that day, while stocks lasted, every two packs of either expansion bought at once came with one of six original holo cards at random, in a small bag: Chikorita, Cyndaquil, Totodile, Mareep, Phanpy or Teddiursa, all drawn by Ken Sugimori. Card shops, Pokémon Centers and most convenience stores took part. Each card has its own illustration and attacks, the logos of both expansions across the picture, and the words 発売記念カード (launch commemoration card).",
